The TextBox control allows users to input text or data via the keyboard. Data retrieved from a TextBox is stored in its Text property as a string.
2. Variables and Data Types
A variable is a named memory location used to store data. In C#, you must declare a variable's data type before using it.
Primitive Data Types:
string: Stores text or sequences of characters.
int: Stores whole numbers (integers).
double: Stores floating-point numbers with standard precision.
decimal: Stores monetary and financial values with high precision.
bool: Stores logical boolean values (true or false).
. String Concatenation & Formatting
The simplest way to join strings or combine text with numbers is using the + operator. You can also format numeric output using the .ToString() method.
7. Constants and Fields
Constants: Variables declared with the const keyword whose values cannot be modified during program execution.
Fields: Variables declared at the class level, making them accessible to all methods within that class
